      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Headache as a side effect of corinfar treatment courses for angina of effort was more commonly seen in patients with pretreatment dystonic rheoencephalographic changes. A single corinfar dose produced a drop of venous tone. Corinfar-associated headache was less common in patients after long-term treatment with high-dose nitroglycerin."},
